# src-tauri/gen/ is DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED — removed 2026-08-16 at KP's ⚛ word.
# Tauri's own scaffold (src-tauri/.gitignore) ignores only /target and
# /gen/schemas, and `tauri android init` writes .gitignore files INSIDE
# gen/android that already exclude build/, .gradle/, *.iml, local.properties
# and keystore.properties. The mobile project is hand-edited ground — manifest,
# themes, MainActivity, launcher icons, gradle config — and belongs in history:
# about 57 tracked files, not the ~900 the folder holds on disk.
# The cost of ignoring it, paid twice: a sibling app's build day cross-landed
# its package identity into a mother repo's gen/android, and git could not see
# it. Echoes sat contaminated four days; Gradle refusing to build was the only
# alarm. Tracked, `git status` names it the moment it happens and
# `git checkout src-tauri/gen/android` heals it in one command.
# Do not re-add it. If build noise appears, the nested gitignores are missing —
# re-run `tauri android init`; never blanket-ignore the parent.

# tools/ is DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED — it was never in this template and was
# added by hand in five repos. A blanket ignore there hid a live and unique
# script (resonance-grammar/tools/export-sql-snippets.mjs) from git entirely:
# no history, no travel with a clone. Ignore a specific binary by name if one
# must stay out — never the folder.

# ─── PYTHON ────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# ─── RUST ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/*

